cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nomibench, please cite the archived release and the paper."
title: "nomibench: calibrated, discoverability-matched benchmarks of gene nominations against genetic causal support"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-06        # TO FILL: the date of the tagged release
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/FarhanHimself/nomibench"
# doi: add the release DOI here once Zenodo has reserved or minted it (RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md)
type: software
authors:                         # TO FILL before the tagged release: affiliation, ORCID and any co-authors, in order
  - family-names: "Payvar"
    given-names: "Mohammad"
keywords:
  - Mendelian randomization
  - SMR
  - Firth logistic regression
  - propensity score
  - plasmode simulation
  - negative controls
  - gene prioritisation
  - Alzheimer's disease
abstract: >-
  Tests whether a set of nominated genes carries more genetic causal support (for example SMR/HEIDI support) than
  its genes' discoverability predicts. Provides a propensity-score Firth estimator with penalised-likelihood
  inference, secondary and doubly robust estimators, estimand-targeted plasmode calibration, discoverability-matched
  negative-control gene sets, a genomic-block bootstrap and pre-specified decision rules.
